From: Jordan Bettcher <thebettcher@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] image: recognise ppc64 in the lightweight-clock dispatch

image/util.h guards the include of a cheap cycle-counter header on the
processor and stops the build with #error on anything it does not know. With
-DIMAGE_SUPPORT=ON the image module is compiled into libhsa-runtime64, so every
translation unit including util.h hits that #error on ppc64le.

The loongarch64 arm is empty and that is the model followed here: the #if only
decides whether a clock header is pulled in, and nothing in the image module
calls __rdtsc(). Verified by compiling the whole module with this arm in place
-- addrlib and all 27 image sources build clean and no undefined reference to
__rdtsc appears.

Should a caller ever appear, the POWER equivalent is
__builtin_ppc_get_timebase(), reading the time base register: a
userspace-readable monotonic counter, the role TSC plays on x86. Checked on
this host, consecutive reads 2046578599920 -> 2046578599924.

Nothing else needed touching. addrlib pulls x86 intrinsics only when
__x86_64__ is defined and hsa-runtime's CMakeLists does not define it -- unlike
runtime/hsa-ext-image/CMakeLists.txt, which hardcodes -D__AMD64__ -D__x86_64__.
That directory is the legacy standalone libhsa-ext-image64.so and is not what
ROCm 10 uses: hsa_ext_interface.cpp calls rocr::image::LoadImage() directly, so
the image code belongs inside libhsa-runtime64.

--- a/runtime/hsa-runtime/image/util.h
+++ b/runtime/hsa-runtime/image/util.h
@@ -78,6 +78,12 @@
 #if defined(__i386__) || defined(__x86_64__)
 #include <x86intrin.h>
 #elif defined(__loongarch64)
+#elif defined(__powerpc64__) || defined(__PPC64__)
+// ppc64, both endiannesses. Nothing to include, exactly as the loongarch64 arm
+// above includes nothing: this #if only guards the lightweight-clock header,
+// and the image module never calls __rdtsc(). Should a caller appear, the POWER
+// equivalent is __builtin_ppc_get_timebase(), reading the userspace-readable
+// time base register.
 #else
 #error                                                                                             \
     "Processor not identified.  " \
